---
title: Card
description: A content container for grouping related information.
---

<ComponentPreview name="p-card-1" />

## Installation

<InstallCommand pnpm="pnpm add @shardsui/svelte" shadcnSvelte="pnpm dlx shadcn-svelte@latest add https://coss-sv.vercel.app/r/card.json" />

## Usage

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import {
    Card,
    CardDescription,
    CardFooter,
    CardHeader,
    CardPanel,
    CardTitle,
  } from "@coss-sv/ui/components/ui/card";
</script>

<Card>
  <CardHeader>
    <CardTitle>Title</CardTitle>
    <CardDescription>Description</CardDescription>
  </CardHeader>
  <CardPanel>Content</CardPanel>
  <CardFooter>Footer</CardFooter>
</Card>
```

### CardFrame with header action

Use `CardFrame` when you need a framed layout with an action button in the header, such as “Add” or
“Connect”:

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import { Add01Icon } from "@hugeicons/core-free-icons";
  import { HugeiconsIcon } from "@hugeicons/svelte";
  import { Button } from "@coss-sv/ui/components/ui/button";
  import {
    Card,
    CardFrame,
    CardFrameAction,
    CardFrameDescription,
    CardFrameHeader,
    CardFrameTitle,
    CardPanel,
  } from "@coss-sv/ui/components/ui/card";
</script>

<CardFrame>
  <CardFrameHeader>
    <CardFrameTitle>Project</CardFrameTitle>
    <CardFrameDescription>Manage your project settings and configuration</CardFrameDescription>
    <CardFrameAction>
      <Button variant="outline">
        <HugeiconsIcon aria-hidden="true" icon={Add01Icon} strokeWidth={2} />
        Add
      </Button>
    </CardFrameAction>
  </CardFrameHeader>
  <Card>
    <CardPanel>Content</CardPanel>
  </Card>
</CardFrame>
```

### CardFrame with a table

For lists or data grids, render a [Table](/docs/components/table) with `variant="card"` inside
`CardFrame` so the grid matches the frame’s border and radius. See the CardFrame example in the Table
docs. Add the table registry item if it is not already in the project.

## API Reference

Card is a native, polymorphic Svelte component family. Each part accepts snippets, native attributes,
a bindable `ref`, `class`, and an `as` prop for changing the rendered element.

### Card

The card root container.

### CardHeader

The header section.

### CardTitle

The card title.

### CardDescription

The supporting description.

### CardAction

A header action container positioned to the right.

### CardPanel

The main content area. `CardContent` is an alias.

### CardFooter

The card footer.

## CardFrame API Reference

`CardFrame` groups a header, content, and footer with consistent styling and clipping. Use it when a
card needs a framed layout with optional header actions.

### CardFrame

The framed card root.

### CardFrameHeader

The frame header.

### CardFrameTitle

The frame title.

### CardFrameDescription

The frame description.

### CardFrameAction

The action container for controls such as “Add” or “Edit”. Place it beside the title and description
inside `CardFrameHeader`; the grid positions it in the top-right corner.

### CardFrameFooter

The frame footer.
